title: 'pallet-proxy: add try_state invariant checks and sort the Proxies map'

doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    In the new `try_state` hook, several storage invariants for the pallet are checked,
    with consideration for future use as an oracle in pallet fuzzing campaigns. The three
    deposit checks warn by default and become hard errors under a new `fuzzing` feature,
    since a live chain can legally hold a stale deposit or an announcement left behind by
    an account migration, neither of which a campaign can produce.

    The sortedness invariant found live state that breaks it: some `Proxies` entries on the
    Polkadot, Kusama and Westend Asset Hubs are unsorted, so `binary_search` misses a
    delegate that is present, leaving the owner unable to remove that proxy or recover its
    deposit while `add_proxy` adds a duplicate instead of failing with `Duplicate`. The
    pallet now declares a storage version and adds `migrations::MigrateV0ToV1`, which sorts
    each entry and drops exact duplicates in a single block. Deposits are left as they are,
    a deduplicated entry pricing below its deposit until `poke_deposit` corrects it.

    The migration is added to every live runtime in this repository that uses the pallet.
    The Rococo runtimes are skipped because that testnet is retired. The Polkadot and Kusama
    Asset Hub runtimes live in `polkadot-fellows/runtimes` and can take it once this is
    released.
- audience: Runtime User
  description: |-
    Accounts whose proxy list was stored out of order can add and remove proxies again after
    the runtime upgrade. A list that held a duplicate is now one entry shorter than the
    deposit recorded for it, and `poke_deposit` returns the difference.

crates:
- name: pallet-proxy
  bump: minor
- name: westend-runtime
  bump: patch
- name: asset-hub-westend-runtime
  bump: patch
- name: collectives-westend-runtime
  bump: patch
- name: coretime-westend-runtime
  bump: patch
- name: people-westend-runtime
  bump: patch
